<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese consumers to get a boost -INE.</title>
<headline>Portuguese consumers to get a boost -INE.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Falling unemployment and increased purchasing power due to lower inflation may stimulate family consumption in the next few months, Portugal's National Statistics Institute (INE) said in its latest economic report.</p>
<p>It said that salaries grew by a nominal average of 3.7 percent during the second quarter of 1997 against an average gain in the consumer price index (CPI) of 1.9 percent.</p>
<p>Two weeks ago the INE reported that unemployment stood at 6.5 percent in the second quarter, compared with 7.3 percent in the previous quarter and 7.2 percent in the second quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>--Lisbon newsroom 3511-353-8254</p>
</text>
